    {
      "id": "claim_f925ec97a1da4477a9c24bda0db5d95a",
      "statement": "AbstractRunnerTLRService.runPipeline starts a new run only when the result is neither present in Redis (DatabaseAccessor.keyExistsInDatabase) nor in flight (CurrentlyRunningRequestsRepository.containsRequest); it dispatches runPipelineAsync via CompletableFuture.supplyAsync and registers the resulting future under the request ID, returns the stored result directly when already cached, and returns Optional.empty otherwise. The check-then-act sequence is not atomic, so concurrent first requests for the same brand-new ID can each dispatch a run before either future is registered.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractRunnerTLRService.java#L83-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8970a414690414eaebc7a829bb88000ee3c01a3e32a4a40ca9a3ffdc0c655735:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_33357e3809cd4902be813c5301698126",
      "statement": "When the async pipeline throws, runPipelineAsync stores a message prefixed with ERROR_PREFIX (the literal string 'Error: ') in Redis and rethrows ArdocoException, so a failed run leaves a retrievable error marker instead of a missing key; a finally block always removes the in-flight entry and deletes the temporary input files on both success and failure paths.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractRunnerTLRService.java#L102-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44663f46d4490d4d47e0a1684038f70084ec073f6b4f0d47534a4d3b380fd4a5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5b8aa40e2da3400494a7ddccb7d9b653",
      "statement": "AbstractService.getResultFromDatabase throws IllegalArgumentException when the key is absent from the database, throws ArdocoException when the stored value is null or starts with the 'Error: ' prefix, and otherwise re-parses the stored JSON's traceLinks and inconsistencies fields into an ArDoCoApiResult; its resultIsInDatabase and resultIsOnItsWay helpers delegate to DatabaseAccessor and CurrentlyRunningRequestsRepository respectively.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractService.java#L58-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5191c707414549109e7d71be94a7ba61b2f7daa798a43689d7347f22611705bb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7da08ee2eab14fc8bb60e4ef13310ec1",
      "statement": "ResultService.getResult returns Optional.empty while the request is still in flight (avoiding a database call) and otherwise reads from Redis; waitForResult blocks on the registered CompletableFuture with a timeout taken from tlr.timeout.seconds (60 seconds by default), returning Optional.empty on timeout and rethrowing ArdocoException on execution or interruption; the family-agnostic ResultController exposes /api/get-result/{id} and /api/wait-for-result/{id}, mapping an empty Optional to 202 Accepted and a present result to 200 OK, so any family's result can be retrieved by ID through these shared endpoints.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/ResultController.java#L33-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c2e725911b0146cd2abd6365542ec5d514bc68b3099cbf403b4a266a285cc9f:"
