    {
      "id": "claim_87b6890c3dc349f0b68642a279d64fa3",
      "statement": "The repository layer splits volatile in-flight tracking from durable storage: CurrentlyRunningRequestsRepository is a singleton-scoped in-memory ConcurrentHashMap of CompletableFuture entries used to skip database calls and to support waiting, while the DatabaseAccessor interface (implemented only by the @Primary RedisAccessor) stores plain string values in Redis, setting each entry with a TTL taken from redis.time-to-live.hours (24 hours by default).",
      "evidence": [
        {
